# Heard — example environment variables (BYOK for self-hosters)
#
# IMPORTANT: nothing in the package loads a `.env` file. Copying this to
# `.env` does NOT configure Heard. The names below only take effect when
# they are EXPORTED in the environment of the process that starts the
# daemon — and the daemon is normally auto-spawned by an agent hook,
# which inherits the agent's environment, not your shell's. So a key
# that works in your terminal usually never reaches the daemon.
#
# The reliable path for every key is:
#
#     heard config set <key> <value>
#
# That writes to the user config dir, which the daemon re-reads on every
# event — so a key takes effect immediately, with no daemon restart.
# Config values also take precedence over the env vars below. The
# packaged .app has no shell env at all, so there it is config-only.
#
# Keep this file as a reference for the env-var NAMES. It is
# documentation, not a config mechanism.

# --- Narration brain (LLM) — bring your own key -------------------------

# Anthropic API key. Used for the narration brain (Claude Haiku) on the
# BYOK path, bypassing the managed api.heard.dev proxy.
# Preferred: heard config set anthropic_api_key <key>
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional OpenAI API key. Alternate narration provider on the BYOK path.
# Preferred: heard config set openai_api_key <key>
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional: override the narration-brain model on the BYOK path only
# (e.g. claude-sonnet-5). Empty/unset -> the default Haiku checkpoint.
# Preferred: heard config set brain_model <model>
# HEARD_BRAIN_MODEL=

# --- Text-to-speech (TTS) — bring your own key --------------------------

# NOTE: the ElevenLabs key is NOT read from the environment at all — the
# daemon reads it from config only (see Daemon._make_tts). Set it with
# `heard config set elevenlabs_api_key <key>` or the menu (Settings ->
# Keys). Without a key, signed-in users use the managed voice proxy, or
# you can download the local Kokoro voice for fully-offline TTS.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=  (config-only, never read from env)

# --- Operational / debug (optional) -------------------------------------

# These two are genuinely env-only — read at process start by whoever
# launches the daemon / hook, with no config equivalent.

# Set to 1 to enable verbose daemon debug logging.
# HEARD_DEBUG=1

# Set to 1 to disable the hook subprocess (used internally to avoid
# recursive narration when the daemon shells out to the CLI). You
# generally do not need to set this yourself.
# HEARD_HOOK_DISABLED=1
